  "description": "*“Father, she dared to harbor lustful thoughts toward my brother.”*\n\nThe horrific scar on her leg, left by a fire when she was a child. Elia, the abbot’s lame daughter, lived as a shadow, shunned by everyone. That is, until her father brought home a mysterious boy he had found in a snowfield. Isaac, her stepbrother, as dazzling as a blessing from God, suddenly burst into her lonely daily life. Her desperate prayer for a “family” that would love her had, before she knew it, twisted into a longing directed toward her brother…\n\n*“I confess the sin of shamelessly craving my brother; judge this sinner according to Your will.”*\n\n(Source: MrBlue, translated)",
